from common import *
it('KERNEL-0134','mechanism','3.3','Spatial indexes (SCL-2; J-K6): each level has (a) static packed indexes (flatbush), partitioned - one partition per arena at L0-L1; at L2-L4 one per district plus one for everything outside districts (hinterland, margin) - each with a tombstone set; and (b) one dynamic uniform grid with O(1) insert and delete.',['§3.3 Spatial indexes'],'kernel',['KERNEL-0016'],['@queries','@indexRebuild','@frozenBase copy'],['static partition','dynamic grid','SCL-2','J-K6'])
it('KERNEL-0135','constant','3.3','Dynamic grid cell size: 25 m at L0-L1, 10 m at L2, 5 m at L3-L4 (table values).',['§3.3 Spatial indexes'],'kernel (table values in @plat/tables)',['@plat/tables'],['@dynamicGrid'],['grid cell 25 m / 10 m / 5 m'])
it('KERNEL-0136','rule','3.3','What each level index holds: the items of that level (current birth level): its vertices; its ROUTE EDGES - each maximal run of that level sub-edges between two vertices of that level or coarser is one item whatever finer vertices later split it, its box the bounding box of the vertices standing on the run when its level batch writes the item, padded by the 0.71 cm hot pixel, and its handle the half-edge leaving its lower (y, x) endpoint (a split keeps that pair on the part at that end, so the handle never changes); and its face records.',['§3.3 What each level index holds'],'kernel',['§2.2 half-edges, birth levels'],['@queries'],['route edge','hot pixel 0.71 cm','handle'])
it('KERNEL-0137','rule','3.3','Route-edge box completeness: the run box holds every finer vertex on it by construction - one placed afterwards lies within the hot pixel of the route edge (§3.6 placement rule (i)), one placed before stands in the box however the route changed since (§3.6 placement bound; J-K32); the endpoints box, padded alike, missed 38 of 400 753 finer vertices under the placement rule non-nearest choices and the run box none (docs/validation/bench/fixall_kernel_r4_checks.out A).',['§3.3 What each level index holds'],'kernel',['@placement','J-K32'],['@queries'],['run box','J-K32'])
it('KERNEL-0138','rule','3.3','Index writes by level: a finer batch that splits a coarser edge with a Steiner vertex writes only its own level index (S10 step (0) and every pooled stage touch only L3 and L4 indexes); a promotion or demotion (the coarser batch own change of a route) moves the vertex or edge to its new level index and rewrites the route-edge items of the levels whose routes it changes: a promoted vertex makes the route edge it now splits two items, a demoted vertex joins its two items into one, a demoted edge leaves its old level item for its new level (§2.2 rule 3).',['§3.3 What each level index holds'],'kernel',['§2.2 rule 3'],['@queries'],['promotion index move','demotion index move'])
it('KERNEL-0139','rule','3.3','No item changes in place (J-K34): every item a batch deletes, re-levels, changes or moves to another partition - deleted vertex, edge or face; promoted or demoted vertex or edge; a route edge whose run a vertex of its level joins or leaves (same-level split, promotion, dissolution, demotion) or a move reshapes; a vertex a move displaces; a face whose own-level ring a re-walk or move changes; an item whose partition changes (every L2-L4 vertex, route edge and face under an L1 face a batch re-owns to another district or to/from the hinterland - S6 regroup, §7.3 - and a vertex on an L1 edge two partitions share when that edge partitions change) - is TOMBSTONED in the static partition its home entry names (Plat.indexHome, §2.2), if it has one (the entry then reads -1), and its successor, if any, is inserted in the grid of its current level; an item already in a grid is deleted or replaced there.',['§3.3 No item changes in place'],'kernel',['§2.2 Plat.indexHome'],['@queries','@tombstone'],['tombstone rule','J-K34','Plat.indexHome'])
it('KERNEL-0140','rule','3.3','Consequence of J-K34: a static item is either exact or filtered, and no query sees an item at its old level, place, extent or partition: a promoted-then-demoted plot-line end answers an L2 query not at all and an L3 query once; a regrouped block plots answer once whichever partitions were rebuilt in between; a regroup leaves both partitions dirty, so the next freeze rebuilds both (pool step 1).',['§3.3 No item changes in place'],'kernel',['@tombstone'],['@queries','@freeze'],['exact or filtered'])
it('KERNEL-0141','mechanism','3.3','Queries: inside a stage every insertion and deletion goes to the grid. A level-n query reads the static partitions of levels <= n its box intersects and their grids, drops each static hit whose item key its partition has tombstoned, expands each route-edge hit into the pieces of its level-n route meeting the box, and returns the vertices of level <= n, each level-n route edge once (as its sub-edge leaving its lower endpoint) and the level-n faces.',['§3.3 Queries'],'kernel',['@staticPartition','@dynamicGrid','@tombstone'],['every stage query','@callbackForm issue order','§7 edit queries'],['queries','level-n query'])
it('KERNEL-0142','rule','3.3','Query result order: sorted by the canonical key of each item kind, read on the query level-n route: a vertex by lattice position (y, then x); an edge by the positions of the two endpoints of its level-n route edge, the lower (y, x) first, never a sub-edge endpoints; a face by the positions of the first two vertices of level <= n on its outer ring - the lowest-leftmost vertex of level <= n and the next vertex of level <= n counter-clockwise, finer vertices skipped, and where the ring visits that vertex twice the smaller of its two successors; in a mixed result vertices before edges before faces. The key is total (no two vertices share a lattice point, no two level-n route edges share both endpoints, a face key is one directed level-n route edge bounding exactly one level-n face), so neither which structure holds an item nor whether a finer level was derived changes any answer (a key read on the full ring reverses two L3 plots once S11 derives L4, fixall_kernel_r3_checks.out C); no implementation needs a slot to break a tie.',['§3.3 Queries'],'kernel',[],['@callbackForm','@slotIndependence','§13.1 slot-renumbering test'],['canonical item key','canonical query order'])
it('KERNEL-0143','term','3.3','Defined term TOMBSTONE: an item key - kind * 2^32 + slot, the kind a vertex, a route edge or a face - held in one set per static partition: the items deleted, moved to another level or partition, or changed since that partition build. Tombstones filter that partition hits only; a new item (the next occupant of a slot freed and reused inside the stage, or an item successor) lives in the dynamic grid, which tombstones never filter, so neither slot reuse nor a level change can hide it and the stale static copy never answers (J-K34).',['§3.3 Tombstones and rebuilds'],'kernel',[],['@queries','@indexRebuild','@overlay'],['tombstone','item key'])
it('KERNEL-0144','mechanism','3.3','Partition rebuild: indexes the live items belonging to the partition - every item of its level in its arena at L0-L1; at L2-L4 the items of its district, a vertex on an L1 edge two partitions share going to the partition with the smaller key (as §3.9 chunks do) - sets their home entries, removes them from the grid and empties its tombstone set.',['§3.3 Tombstones and rebuilds'],'kernel',['@staticPartition'],['@freeze','@merge'],['indexRebuild','partition rebuild'])
it('KERNEL-0145','constant','3.3','Home column: 2 B per vertex, edge-pair and face slot (about 0.5 MB at a finished CITY); lets a batch tombstone an item without searching the partitions.',['§3.3 Tombstones and rebuilds','§3.3 pool step 1 (2 B per slot)'],'kernel (Plat.indexHome field in §2.2)',['§2.2 Plat.indexHome'],['@tombstone','@frozenBase copy'],['home column','indexHome'])
it('KERNEL-0146','rule','3.3','Static partitions are rebuilt at three moments, never per batch: (1) when a stage ends - an eager stage once after its last batch; S10 eager step (0) once before the pool freeze; a lazy or pooled per-district stage, the district own partitions after that district run; (2) during an editing session, when a partition grid overflow exceeds max(256, 1/4 of its static size) - a count, never an idle timer; (3) at every pool freeze, for the partitions edits left dirty (pool step 1).',['§3.3 Tombstones and rebuilds','§3.3 pool step 1'],'kernel',['@indexRebuild'],['§4 stage end','§7 editing session','@freeze'],['three rebuild moments','max(256, 1/4)'])
it('KERNEL-0147','budget','3.3','Measured flatbush construction (docs/validation/bench/bench_index.out): 0.24 ms at 1 000 items, 2.3 ms at 8 000, 4.9 ms at 17 000; at CITY about one L3 and one L4 rebuild per stage (about 7 ms together) or about 0.2-0.3 ms per district partition, where a rebuild per block or per plot commit would cost 1.9 s (S10) and 13.4 s (S11). A single plot edit rebuilds at most its district L3 and L4 partitions (<= 1 000 items each, about 0.5 ms), inside §12.6 plot-edit budget.',['§3.3 Tombstones and rebuilds'],'kernel (budget §12.6)',['bench_index.out'],['§12.6 plot-edit budget'],['flatbush cost'])
it('KERNEL-0148','test','3.3','§13.2 cost-model test fails if rebuild work grows with the number of commits.',['§3.3 Tombstones and rebuilds'],'§13.2 testing',['@indexRebuild'],[],['cost-model test'])
